      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>So how was everyone&#39;s Origins?&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>What&#39;d you do?&nbsp; What&#39;d you play?&nbsp; What&#39;d you eat?&nbsp; What&#39;d you buy?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As mentioned earlier, I spent most of my Origins running&nbsp;<em>Cold Steel Wardens&nbsp;</em>and the rpg I currently have in alpha,&nbsp;<em>De Civitates Dei</em>.&nbsp; I did manage to play a few games:&nbsp; a Quantum Black game (which uses the Ubiquity mechanics), an ICONS game, and a Savage Worlds Stargate game.&nbsp; I had two others scheduled, but I was the only person to show for the first and my wife and I skipped the second in favor of some much-needed downtime.</p><p>I also had a pitch meeting with Indie Boards and Cards for a new card game I&#39;ve been working on.&nbsp; While the original person I&#39;d been talking to wasn&#39;t particularly interested, the fellow he brought along (who happened to be their acquisitions manager) was really enamored with my design and wants to see more, as I continue playtesting.&nbsp; Small victory, definitely!</p><p>I actually made a point to not buy anything this time around, as we&#39;ve been trying to cut back on unnecessary spending.&nbsp; I was tempted by a few items, but nothing blew me away to the point where I &quot;had&quot; to have it.&nbsp; Was hoping that Green Ronin might possibly have Faces of Thedas in, but it&#39;s been pushed back until after GenCon.</p><p>While Columbus&#39; storied North Market is always great, we always try to get to some of the new restaurants in the Short North.&nbsp; The Eagle (north as you walk up High Street) may well have the best fried chicken I&#39;ve ever eaten; get it with the white cheddar grits, which are just phenomenal.&nbsp; The Flat Iron Bar &amp; Diner (near the Red Roof) has a pretty solid pulled pork, but their jalapeno cornbread--which comes sliced like a massive piece of sheet cake, with a giant dollop of honey-butter like icing--really stole the show.&nbsp; Other highlights included the massive quesadilla from Fuzzy&#39;s Taco Shop and the duck-fat frites from Taste of Belgium.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
